Subject: [PATCH] crypto: eip93 - fix IRQF_ONESHOT without a thread handler

The driver registers a hard IRQ handler with IRQF_ONESHOT but passes
a NULL thread_fn. Linux 7.3 warns about this combination in
request_threaded_irq():

  WARNING: kernel/irq/manage.c:1503 at __setup_irq+0x108/0x8d4
  Modules linked in: crypto_hw_eip93(+)

The handler only masks the interrupt and schedules a tasklet, so it
does not need a threaded handler. Use devm_request_irq() instead.

---

--- a/drivers/crypto/inside-secure/eip93/eip93-main.c
+++ b/drivers/crypto/inside-secure/eip93/eip93-main.c
@@ -430,9 +430,8 @@
 	if (eip93->irq < 0)
 		return eip93->irq;
 
-	ret = devm_request_threaded_irq(eip93->dev, eip93->irq, eip93_irq_handler,
-					NULL, IRQF_ONESHOT,
-					dev_name(eip93->dev), eip93);
+	ret = devm_request_irq(eip93->dev, eip93->irq, eip93_irq_handler,
+			       0, dev_name(eip93->dev), eip93);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
